! Test v1.09.2 (1/2): symmetry-blocked numerical Hessian.
! CH4 HF/STO-3G, Td: 2 symmetry-unique of 5 atoms -> the FD loop
! computes 12 of 30 displaced gradients and reconstructs the rest by
!     H(perm_g(C), a) = R_g * H(C, rep) * R_g^T .
! Expected (container reference, gfortran 13.3, netlib BLAS):
!   * startup line "Point group: Td";
!   * announce "2 symmetry-unique of 5 atoms; computing 12 of 30";
!   * frequencies IDENTICAL to the %hess_nosym full-FD run at all
!     printed digits, with exact degeneracies:
!       1689.45 (t2, x3)  1907.72 (e, x2)  3470.25 (a1)
!       3726.98 (t2, x3)  cm-1
!   * measured speedup 2.4x (theoretical 30/12 = 2.5x).
! The %hess_nosym twin of this input is numerics-bit-identical to
! the pristine pre-1.09.2 full displacement loop.
%method  HF
%basis   sto-3g
%job     freq
%hess_method numerical
*geometry angstrom
 C   0.000000    0.000000    0.000000
 H   0.629118    0.629118    0.629118
 H  -0.629118   -0.629118    0.629118
 H  -0.629118    0.629118   -0.629118
 H   0.629118   -0.629118   -0.629118
*end
